<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ERA borrows 1,360 tonnes of uranium.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ERA borrows 1,360 tonnes of uranium.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian uranium miner Energy Resources of Australia Ltd (ERA) said on Tuesday it had signed a loan agreement for 1,360 tonnes of uranium concentrate from one its substantial shareholders.</p>
<p>The company, which is controlled by mining house North Ltd, said it would draw down between 957 tonnes and 1,360 tonnes over an 18 month period beginning this month and repay the loan over four years from 2003.</p>
</text>
